    "created_at": "2024-09-24T08:58:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-09-24T08:58:11Z",
    "body": "> This isn't viable for the same reason we don't support screenshots. That would leak information about what is displayed on the page.\r\n\r\nAgree with @flashymittens, \r\n\r\n`window.exportPdf(<OptionalDomNode>)` which will export Given Dom as an argument.\r\n\r\nAlso people can use `@media print` to control the display of data.\r\n\r\nMany peoples are already using client side PDF generations using different third party libraries([jsPDF usage stats](https://trends.builtwith.com/javascript/jsPDF)), And it is application's responsibility to control what should be visible and what should not.\r\n\r\nFrom browser's API point of view we can control generic security concerns (**for example**: Restricted access to this API from browser plugins etc.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2370680675/reactions",
