    "created_at": "2025-02-03T01:42:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-03T01:53:05Z",
    "body": "Agreed, this would be a highly valuable addition to the standard browser APIs.\n\nCurrently, client-side PDF generation often requires paid [third-party libraries](https://www.telerik.com/kendo-react-ui/components/pdfprocessing), which may lack full support for essential features like custom fonts, limiting their usefulness.\n\nThe alternative—rendering the same DOM on a server using a headless browser—is both resource-intensive (requiring an additional browser instance) and raises privacy concerns, as it necessitates transmitting customer data outside the user’s browser.\n\nA native window.exportPdf() API would greatly simplify this process, improving performance, privacy, and accessibility for web applications.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2629711525/reactions",
