    "created_at": "2025-08-28T00:53:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-28T00:53:31Z",
    "body": "Hi @domenic ,\n\nI think it would be worth re-opening [#7946](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7946). While related, the scope of this proposal is distinct from [#10612](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10612).\n\n- #10612 is focused on adding an option to export the print output (e.g. PDF) directly to a buffer, enabling developers to capture and process the rendered document programmatically. A key aspect is avoiding user interaction with a print dialog entirely.\n- #7946, on the other hand, was more about providing better control over the print pipeline itself.\n\nThe difference is subtle but important: this isn’t about changing user prompts or print dialogs, but rather enabling a programmatic export flow that developers can integrate into automated workflows. That capability still seems valuable and not fully addressed by #10612.\n\nWould you consider re-opening #7946 so the discussion can continue separately?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
